So both API-level reasoning AND tag-based reasoning end up as `reasoning` type in the output. The processing loop accumulates all of them in `thinkingContent`. This could mean that a model that uses BOTH `reasoning_content` AND `<think>` tags in text content would have reasoning content doubled.

But this is probably an edge case that doesn't happen in practice. Most models use one or the other.

